e has already nearly doubled to 5.5  percent if we carry on with this total  shutdown some predict we'll see  unemployment rise to 30%  you think this is all just abstract  statistics listen to the mayor the  sheriff of Knox County Tennessee this  week over the past 48 hours that office  has now examined nine suspected suicides  eight of which are from Knox County  alone four Knox County that's almost 10  percent of last year's total number in  the past two days alone that number is  utterly shocking and makes me wonder is  what we are doing now really the best  approach how can we respond to Coba 19  in a way that keeps our economy intact  keeps people employed and empowers our  people with the feeling of hope and  optimism not desperation and despair  it's not just the corona virus that  kills people poverty kills despair kills  if this total shot down goes on too long  it will kill more people than  coronavirus you just won't see the  numbers in a neat little box on cable  news I'm so sick of irresponsible idiots  on TV pretending this is all so simple  save every life well if you really want  to save every life then take seriously  the death rate from the total shutdown  acknowledge the pain and suffering of  millions of struggling Americans for  whom the people on TV seem to show no  understanding or empathy flatten the  curve not the economy obviously doesn't  mean pretend the virus doesn't exist and  lift all restrictions overnight no one's  saying ignore public health we're saying  that the virus and the shot down both  hurt public health so we need to balance  the two and here's how it's a simple  message open where possible closed where  necessary we now have a month more to  slow the spread let's make it count  but as we do let's push the public  health officials to develop a plan that  is more targeted and surgical than a  total shutdown  we have the data to identify the people  most at risk of needing hospital  treatment protect them if you're older  with a serious underlying health  condition  should stay home compulsory quarantine  protect vulnerable places an all-out  effort to help New York City New Orleans  and emerging hotspots with the equipment  and resources they need but also protect  the places that are relatively  unaffected so they can open up a rural  Idaho County became a hot spot because  of wealthy visitors fleeing places like  New York and Seattle that is not okay  quite rightly the White House has now  implemented a travel advisory to stop  that kind of spread and I hope we see  more even during the next month and  certainly afterwards the right strategy  to reduce the coronavirus death rate and  the shot down death rate is open where  possible closed where necessary  that would mean keeping the ban on large  gatherings but it could also mean for  example opening up workplaces just with  temperature checks for all workers by  the way this is completely in line with  what the doctor Falchi has said you find  after a period of time that there are  areas that are very different from other  areas of the country you may not want to  essentially treat it as it just one  force for the entire country  but look like flexibility in different  areas flexibility in different areas  open where possible closed where  necessary to enable that flexibility  will need to continue the rapid progress  in testing so we can decide place by  place where it's possible to open up and  where it's necessary to stay closed but  the vital thing the president did last  week was to change the conversation from  the despair of indefinite shutdown to  the hope of careful reopening he put a  light at the end of the tunnel so in  this extra month of shot-down  let's commit to a new phase in this  fight more targeted more surgical more  balanced open where possible closed  where necessary that's the way to  flatten the curve without flattening the  economy
 

